; When a transaction exchanges two commodities without a cost, and its
; first posting holds neither of them, Ledger prices the commodity that
; entered the transaction's balance first.  Ledger adds up the real
; postings in order; at the first posting in a second commodity, the sum
; of the postings before it enters first unless it is zero, and a zero
; sum leaves the choice to the first non-zero posting from there on.
; These transactions pin the edges of that rule that
; xact-price-inference-cancel-first.test does not.
;
; The first bills ten hours after a two-hour correction.  Hours are kept
; as seconds, so its first posting, in hours, holds neither commodity;
; the correction sums to zero before the dollars arrive, so the dollars
; enter first and are priced in time, at 24s, as a lot on
; Income:Consulting.  The second reaches its first AUD posting, a zero
; fee, when the ZAR transfer has summed to zero: nothing enters there,
; and the first non-zero posting after it is in ZAR, so ZAR is priced in
; AUD although an AUD posting came before it.  The third reaches its first
; NOK posting, again a zero fee, before the SEK transfer has cancelled:
; the 50 SEK enter first and stay first after the transfer cancels, so
; SEK is priced in NOK.  ZAR and SEK sort after the other currency, so a
; fixed order of the two commodities would price AUD and NOK.  Each
; transaction uses its own pair, so that no commodity is already a price
; target (#1130).  Ledger 3.4.1 made the same three choices.

2024/01/05 Billing after a correction
    Assets:Time               2h
    Expenses:Time            -2h
    Income:Consulting     $-1500
    Assets:Billable          10h

2024/01/06 Exchange after a transfer and a zero fee
    [Budget:Travel]          $100
    [Budget:Available]      $-100
    Assets:Wallet:ZAR        50 ZAR
    Assets:Bank:ZAR         -50 ZAR
    Expenses:Fees             0 AUD
    Assets:Bank:ZAR        -115 ZAR
    Assets:AUD              100 AUD

2024/01/07 Exchange with a fee posted between the transfer legs
    [Budget:Travel]          $100
    [Budget:Available]      $-100
    Assets:Wallet:SEK        50 SEK
    Expenses:Fees             0 NOK
    Assets:Bank:SEK         -50 SEK
    Assets:NOK              100 NOK
    Assets:Bank:SEK        -115 SEK

test pricedb
P 2024/01/05 00:00:00 $ 24s
P 2024/01/06 00:00:00 ZAR 0.869565 AUD
P 2024/01/07 00:00:00 SEK 0.869565 NOK
end test

test bal --lots --flat --no-total Assets Income
             100 AUD  Assets:AUD
-165 SEK {0.869565 NOK} [2024/01/07]  Assets:Bank:SEK
-165 ZAR {0.869565 AUD} [2024/01/06]  Assets:Bank:ZAR
              10.00h  Assets:Billable
             100 NOK  Assets:NOK
               2.00h  Assets:Time
50 SEK {0.869565 NOK} [2024/01/07]  Assets:Wallet:SEK
50 ZAR {0.869565 AUD} [2024/01/06]  Assets:Wallet:ZAR
$-1500 {24s} [2024/01/05]  Income:Consulting
end test
